  partName: Spark Plug
  description: The Spark Plug is a tiny, elongated plug located at the top-center-front
    of the engine, responsible for igniting the fuel-air mixture inside the combustion
    chamber. Its primary function is to generate a high-voltage spark, enabling efficient
    combustion and power generation. Interestingly, the Spark Plug's material, Material.002,
    is designed to withstand extreme temperatures and corrosion, ensuring reliable
    spark generation and engine performance.
